.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt LIBCUDA 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libcuda
.Nd native CUDA Driver API device and context subset
.Sh LIBRARY
libcuda
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In cuda.h
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuInit "unsigned int flags"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDriverGetVersion "int *driverVersion"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDeviceGetCount "int *count"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDeviceGet "CUdevice *device" "int ordinal"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDeviceGetName "char *name" "int len" "CUdevice dev"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDeviceGetUuid "CUuuid *uuid" "CUdevice dev"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDeviceTotalMem "size_t *bytes" "CUdevice dev"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDeviceGetAttribute "int *pi" "CUdevice_attribute attrib" "CUdevice dev"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDevicePrimaryCtxRetain "CUcontext *pctx" "CUdevice dev"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuDevicePrimaryCtxRelease "CUdevice dev"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuCtxGetCurrent "CUcontext *pctx"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuCtxSetCurrent "CUcontext ctx"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuCtxGetDevice "CUdevice *device"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuGetErrorName "CUresult error" "const char **pStr"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuGetErrorString "CUresult error" "const char **pStr"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuGetProcAddress "const char *symbol" "void **pfn" "int cudaVersion" "cuuint64_t flags"
.Ft CUresult
.Fn cuGetProcAddress_v2 "const char *symbol" "void **pfn" "int cudaVersion" "cuuint64_t flags" "CUdriverProcAddressQueryResult *symbolStatus"
.Ft const char *
.Fn cudaNativeGetBackendName void
.Ft int
.Fn cudaNativeProviderKnown "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn cudaNativeFakeProfileKnown "const char *name" "size_t length"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library provides a small, native FreeBSD subset of the CUDA Driver API.
It uses neither the Linux compatibility layer nor NVIDIA's CUDA libraries.
The public header is
.In cuda.h .
.Dv CUDA_VERSION
is 13000 and
.Dv CUDA_NATIVE_VERSION
is 100, encoding version 0.1.0 as major * 10000 + minor * 100 + patch.
The C declarations are also enclosed in C++ linkage guards.
All exported functions have the provisional symbol version
.Dv CUDA_1.0 .
.Pp
.Fn cuInit
accepts only zero flags and initializes the provider registry once per process.
Device and context calls other than argument validation require successful
initialization; before it they return
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED .
.Fn cuDriverGetVersion ,
the error queries, and
.Fn cuGetProcAddress
do not require initialization.
.Ss Providers
.Ev CUDA_NATIVE_BACKEND
selects
.Dq fake
or
.Dq nvrm .
The default is
.Dq nvrm .
An unknown name makes
.Fn cuInit
fail with
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE .
The nvrm provider is a stub in this release: enumeration returns
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED
and no device is opened.
.Pp
The fake provider defaults to one synthetic GB206 device.
.Ev CUDA_NATIVE_FAKE_PROFILE
accepts a comma-separated list of
.Dq gb206
and
.Dq gb10 .
The list
.Dq gb206,gb10
provides GB206 followed by GB10.
An unknown or empty profile is an invalid value.
Fake names, UUIDs, memory sizes, and attributes are test data, not hardware
measurements.
.Ss Native extension queries
.Fn cudaNativeGetBackendName
returns the value of
.Ev CUDA_NATIVE_BACKEND
when set, or the library's default provider name otherwise.
.Fn cudaNativeProviderKnown
returns nonzero only when its argument names a registered provider.
.Fn cudaNativeFakeProfileKnown
returns nonzero only when the specified byte string names a fake profile in the
library's profile table.
These cuda-native extensions do not initialize a provider.
.Fn cudaNativeGetBackendName
reads the calling process's environment when it is called, so its answer
follows
.Ev CUDA_NATIVE_BACKEND
and can change inside one process.
Provider and profile table membership is fixed by the loaded library and does
not depend on the environment.
.Ss Devices
Device ordinals are contiguous in their visible enumeration order.
Invalid ordinals return
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_DEVICE .
.Fn cuDeviceGetName
always terminates the destination and truncates a name to fit.
.Fn cuDeviceTotalMem
returns bytes.
.Fn cuDeviceGetAttribute
returns
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED
for an attribute outside the subset and leaves the destination unchanged.
.Ss Visibility
.Ev CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES
is read during the first initialization attempt.
The outcome of that attempt, including failure, is permanent for the process
lifetime; later environment changes do not retry initialization.
When unset, every provider device is visible in physical order.
When set to an empty string, no device is visible.
Otherwise it is a comma-separated sequence of zero-based physical indices or
UUID selectors of the form
.Dq GPU-<uuid> .
Entries filter and reorder the visible list.
An invalid index ends parsing, so only entries before it are visible.
UUID selectors may be unambiguous prefixes of the canonical UUID text.
An invalid or ambiguous UUID selector also ends parsing in this implementation.
A repeated physical device is an invalid entry and ends parsing, so each visible
ordinal has a distinct device identity.
When no devices remain visible,
.Fn cuInit
returns
.Dv CUDA_SUCCESS
and
.Fn cuDeviceGetCount
reports zero.
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_NO_DEVICE
is not returned for an empty device set.
MIG selectors are not implemented.
.Ss Context state
.Fn cuDevicePrimaryCtxRetain
retains one reference-counted primary context per physical device.
Retaining an already active primary context returns the same handle.
It does not make that context current.
.Fn cuDevicePrimaryCtxRelease
releases one reference; releasing an inactive primary context returns
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_CONTEXT .
The final release invalidates the handle, which may be reused by a later retain.
.Pp
The current context is per thread and initially null.
.Fn cuCtxSetCurrent
accepts null or an active primary context owned by this library.
.Fn cuCtxGetCurrent
returns the calling thread's current handle.
.Fn cuCtxGetDevice
returns the visible ordinal associated with that handle, or
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_CONTEXT
when no active context is current.
These calls manage user-space state only; they do not submit GPU work.
.Ss Errors and entry points
.Fn cuGetErrorName
and
.Fn cuGetErrorString
return static text for each
.Vt CUresult
value defined by this subset.
An unknown result or null output pointer returns
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE .
An unknown result also sets
.Va *pStr
to null.
.Pp
.Fn cuGetProcAddress_v2
looks up the library's public entry points in one table.
The header maps the source-level name
.Fn cuGetProcAddress
to this five-argument function.
The dynamic symbol
.Fn cuGetProcAddress
retains the documented four-argument CUDA 11.3 interface for legacy callers.
Both forms accept default, legacy-stream, and per-thread-default-stream flags.
.Pp
A request for a CUDA version newer than
.Dv CUDA_VERSION
returns
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE
and sets a supplied query status to
.Dv CU_GET_PROC_ADDRESS_VERSION_NOT_SUFFICIENT .
Every listed entry point is available when querying
.Dv CUDA_VERSION
(13000).
This implementation does not assign historical introduction versions to
individual entry points; a lower requested version does not by itself suppress
a table entry.
An unknown name returns
.Dv CUDA_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ,
sets the function pointer to null, and sets a supplied status to
.Dv CU_GET_PROC_ADDRESS_SYMBOL_NOT_FOUND .
The unknown-name result is intentionally stricter than the success-with-null-pointer
behavior in the current public reference.
Every failed entry-point query sets
.Va *pfn
to null when that pointer is supplied; the current form also updates a supplied
.Va symbolStatus .
The current form accepts a null
.Va symbolStatus
when the caller does not need the query result.
These writes are exceptions to the general unchanged-output rule below.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions return
.Dv CUDA_SUCCESS
on success or a
.Vt CUresult
error value.
Unless documented otherwise, output pointers must not be null and are not
changed on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cuda-native-info 1 ,
.Xr pthread 3
.Sh HISTORY
This clean-room subset first appeared in cuda-native 0.1.0.
Its provider ABI and symbol version remain provisional until the first package
release.
